1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,630
A skater spins faster as
she pulls her arms in.

2
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:06,552
A diver curls into a
ball and flips faster.

3
00:00:06,952 --> 00:00:08,225
Nobody pushes them.

4
00:00:08,225 --> 00:00:09,885
Yet their spin speeds up.

5
00:00:10,335 --> 00:00:12,218
Diya tries it on a spinning chair.

6
00:00:12,218 --> 00:00:13,806
Arms out, she turns slowly.

7
00:00:14,156 --> 00:00:17,611
She pulls her arms in, and
suddenly she whirls around.

8
00:00:17,611 --> 00:00:19,902
Where did the extra spin come from?

9
00:00:20,402 --> 00:00:23,421
The answer is one of the
biggest rules in physics.

10
00:00:24,021 --> 00:00:27,235
Angular momentum is the
amount of spin a body carries.

11
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,502
We write it as L.

12
00:00:28,852 --> 00:00:33,317
For a body turning about a fixed
axis, L equals I times omega.

13
00:00:33,717 --> 00:00:36,771
I says how the mass is
spread around the axis.

14
00:00:36,771 --> 00:00:38,768
Omega says how fast it turns.

15
00:00:39,168 --> 00:00:42,843
And the rule: if no outside
torque acts, L cannot change.

16
00:00:42,843 --> 00:00:44,133
It stays the same.

17
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:46,583
Our motion notebook, from above.

18
00:00:46,583 --> 00:00:49,378
Diya on the chair, holding
a weight in each hand.

19
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:53,383
Arms out, the weights are point
eight metres from the axis.

20
00:00:53,383 --> 00:00:54,860
I is four point five.

21
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:57,139
She turns at two radians per second.

22
00:00:57,539 --> 00:01:00,216
So L is four point five times two.

23
00:01:00,216 --> 00:01:01,116
Nine.

24
00:01:01,233 --> 00:01:04,507
Now she pulls the weights
in, to point two metres.

25
00:01:04,507 --> 00:01:06,319
I falls to one point five.

26
00:01:06,719 --> 00:01:08,000
Watch omega climb.

27
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,565
Two, three, four, and up
to six radians per second.

28
00:01:11,965 --> 00:01:12,865
And L?

29
00:01:12,646 --> 00:01:14,476
One point five times six.

30
00:01:14,476 --> 00:01:15,412
Still nine.

31
00:01:15,412 --> 00:01:19,184
On the graph, the L line
stays flat while omega rises.

32
00:01:19,684 --> 00:01:20,584
Slow-mo replay.

33
00:01:20,576 --> 00:01:22,512
Freeze in the middle of the pull.

34
00:01:22,862 --> 00:01:25,322
Her hands pull each weight
straight towards the axis.

35
00:01:25,722 --> 00:01:29,204
A pull that points at the
axis has no turning effect.

36
00:01:29,204 --> 00:01:30,613
Its torque is zero.

37
00:01:31,013 --> 00:01:33,630
No outside torque, so L stays fixed.

38
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:36,318
I went down, so omega had to go up.

39
00:01:36,918 --> 00:01:39,211
Here is the reasoning, link by link.

40
00:01:39,561 --> 00:01:41,835
Nothing outside twists the chair.

41
00:01:41,835 --> 00:01:43,437
So L stays the same.

42
00:01:43,837 --> 00:01:45,133
L is I times omega.

43
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:48,018
Pulling in the weights
makes I three times smaller.

44
00:01:48,418 --> 00:01:52,579
To keep the product the same, omega
must become three times bigger.

45
00:01:52,579 --> 00:01:53,736
Two becomes six.

46
00:01:54,336 --> 00:01:56,428
Now the rule, one step at a time.

47
00:01:56,778 --> 00:01:57,678
Step one.

48
00:01:57,494 --> 00:01:59,608
Each bit carries m r squared omega.

49
00:01:59,608 --> 00:02:00,552
Add them all.

50
00:02:00,552 --> 00:02:01,722
L equals I omega.

51
00:02:02,472 --> 00:02:03,372
Step two.

52
00:02:03,196 --> 00:02:06,155
The rate of change of L
equals the outside torque.

53
00:02:06,905 --> 00:02:07,864
Step three.

54
00:02:07,864 --> 00:02:11,647
If the outside torque is
zero, d L by d t is zero.

55
00:02:11,647 --> 00:02:13,044
So L is constant.

56
00:02:13,794 --> 00:02:14,716
Step four.

57
00:02:14,716 --> 00:02:17,843
So I one omega one equals I two omega two.

58
00:02:18,593 --> 00:02:19,493
Step five.

59
00:02:19,427 --> 00:02:22,744
Spin energy can be written
as L squared over two I.

60
00:02:22,744 --> 00:02:25,208
Same L, smaller I, so more energy.

61
00:02:25,958 --> 00:02:27,043
Remember this.

62
00:02:27,043 --> 00:02:30,784
With no outside torque, angular
momentum stays the same.

63
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:32,641
Side by side.

64
00:02:32,641 --> 00:02:36,174
Arms out: I is four
point five, omega is two.

65
00:02:36,174 --> 00:02:37,169
L is nine.

66
00:02:37,569 --> 00:02:40,735
Arms in: I is one point
five, omega is six.

67
00:02:40,735 --> 00:02:42,012
L is still nine.

68
00:02:42,612 --> 00:02:43,612
Now you try.

69
00:02:43,612 --> 00:02:48,227
When she pulls her arms in, does her
spin energy stay the same, go up,

70
00:02:48,227 --> 00:02:49,179
or go down?

71
00:02:49,179 --> 00:02:50,422
Pause and decide.

72
00:02:53,622 --> 00:02:54,522
It goes up!

73
00:02:54,454 --> 00:02:56,323
Nine joules becomes twenty seven.

74
00:02:56,323 --> 00:02:59,991
Her arm muscles did eighteen joules
of work pulling the weights in.

75
00:03:00,641 --> 00:03:01,732
One more twist.

76
00:03:01,732 --> 00:03:04,635
Arms out, she simply
lets go of both weights.

77
00:03:05,035 --> 00:03:07,861
Does she speed up, like
when she pulled them in?

78
00:03:07,861 --> 00:03:08,941
Pause and decide.

79
00:03:12,041 --> 00:03:12,941
No!

80
00:03:12,481 --> 00:03:15,642
Each weight flies off with
its own share of spin.

81
00:03:15,642 --> 00:03:19,405
Her L drops along with her
I, so her omega stays at two.

82
00:03:20,055 --> 00:03:21,746
Now, one worked example.

83
00:03:22,096 --> 00:03:26,605
A disc with I equal to four turns
freely at ten radians per second.

84
00:03:26,605 --> 00:03:30,951
A ring with I equal to one, not
spinning, is dropped onto it.

85
00:03:30,951 --> 00:03:32,352
They turn together.

86
00:03:32,352 --> 00:03:35,226
Find the new omega, and the energy lost.

87
00:03:35,726 --> 00:03:38,218
No outside torque, so L is kept.

88
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,058
Four times ten is forty.

89
00:03:40,808 --> 00:03:42,489
Together, I is five.

90
00:03:42,489 --> 00:03:44,614
So omega is forty over five.

91
00:03:44,614 --> 00:03:46,453
Eight radians per second.

92
00:03:47,203 --> 00:03:50,862
Energy before: one half
times four times ten squared.

93
00:03:50,862 --> 00:03:52,289
Two hundred joules.

94
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:56,682
Energy after: one half times
five times eight squared.

95
00:03:56,682 --> 00:03:58,295
One hundred and sixty.

96
00:03:58,295 --> 00:04:01,897
So forty joules are lost,
as heat, when they grip.

97
00:04:02,547 --> 00:04:04,009
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:04:04,359 --> 00:04:07,724
Many students think a faster
spin always means a torque acted.

99
00:04:08,124 --> 00:04:09,024
Not here.

100
00:04:08,882 --> 00:04:10,501
No torque acted on Diya.

101
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:14,034
I went down, so omega went
up, and L stayed the same.

102
00:04:14,684 --> 00:04:16,058
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:16,058 --> 00:04:20,182
In skaters and divers, bodies dropped
onto turning discs, and a planet

104
00:04:20,182 --> 00:04:21,603
or star that shrinks.

105
00:04:22,203 --> 00:04:23,352
Exam level now.

106
00:04:23,352 --> 00:04:27,909
Suppose the Earth shrank to half its
radius, keeping its mass, and stayed

107
00:04:27,909 --> 00:04:29,155
a uniform sphere.

108
00:04:29,155 --> 00:04:31,015
How long would one day be?

109
00:04:31,015 --> 00:04:32,212
Pause and solve.

110
00:04:37,612 --> 00:04:39,104
The answer is A.

111
00:04:39,104 --> 00:04:40,109
Six hours.

112
00:04:40,609 --> 00:04:43,975
For a uniform sphere, I
is two fifths MR squared.

113
00:04:43,975 --> 00:04:46,344
Half the radius makes I one quarter.

114
00:04:46,844 --> 00:04:49,561
L is kept, so omega
becomes four times bigger.

115
00:04:50,061 --> 00:04:52,368
The day is the time for one turn.

116
00:04:52,368 --> 00:04:55,207
It becomes one quarter
of twenty four hours.

117
00:04:55,207 --> 00:04:56,107
Six hours.

118
00:04:56,651 --> 00:04:58,191
Here is your recap.

119
00:04:58,191 --> 00:04:59,773
Screenshot this card.

120
00:05:02,973 --> 00:05:04,912
Can you answer these without help?

121
00:05:05,312 --> 00:05:06,212
One.

122
00:05:05,711 --> 00:05:08,501
Why does Diya spin faster
when she pulls her arms in?

123
00:05:09,401 --> 00:05:10,301
Two.

124
00:05:09,876 --> 00:05:13,484
Why does her spin energy go
up, though L stays the same?

125
00:05:14,384 --> 00:05:15,284
Three.

126
00:05:14,828 --> 00:05:17,383
Why does letting go of the
weights not speed her up?

127
00:05:18,283 --> 00:05:21,242
Next time: a cycle wheel
rolls down the road.

128
00:05:21,242 --> 00:05:25,275
Its top races ahead, yet its
bottom point is not moving at all.

129
00:05:25,275 --> 00:05:26,175
How?

130
00:05:25,756 --> 00:05:26,811
Rolling motion.
